  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Private Sector Development and Competitiveness Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objective is to build capacity of public and private sector actors from relevant ministries, departments and agencies of the government (esp those in Finance and various utility/infrastructure sectors), and from private sector entrepreneurs/enterprise managers (members of the Federation of Congolese Enterprises, along with SME and sector-specialized trade associations) in the application of the framework of the new Public Procurement Law governing award of contracts for Public-Private Partnership (PPP) arrangements and other forms of public works using a competitive bidding process. This project will concentrate on (1) developing project design and management instruments, (2) creating and equipping regional resource centers for capacity building, and (3)providing training to improve the comprehension of the legal and regulative framework for public procurement, in practical aspects to be able to apply the framework, especially to competently participate in the competitive award/bidding process; in the means of compliance and use of prior and post-review/audit of procurement decision mechanisms; understanding of the process for control and complaints handling-- all of which leading to increased accountability of key players and the demand for good governance in DRC.</narrative>
  </description>
